    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 53 tests run with 0 failures, including `Cp39Tests` (the tenure-cap test).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented tenure-driven membership level 4 while keeping new owners capped at level 3.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.membershipLevel(Owner)`** \u2014 Added a fourth factor: the owner earns +1 when tenure (days from `registrationDate` to today, via `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between`) exceeds 365. The pre-tenure factors (base 1 + email + zero namesakes) still cap at 3, so:\n- A brand-new owner has `registrationDate == today` \u2192 0 tenure \u2192 the tenure factor never fires \u2192 even with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` (and any household size) it lands at level 3, never 4.\n- Only an owner tenured beyond 365 days can reach level 4. The cap is now `Math.min(level, 4)`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `membershipLevel` schema: `maximum` 3 \u2192 4 and the description to document the tenure factor and that new owners never exceed 3.\n\nThe existing `Cp39Tests` (new owner with email + no namesake \u2192 level 3) and all other membership tests (Cp15, Cp23, Cp24) remain green.",
